README.OSK -- what was changed to build CMDS/screenscandir.c: `filecnt' is now set to 0.  The original declares it`register int filecnt;' and never initialises it, then stores each fileit accepts at dirlist[filecnt++] -- so the first store went wherever theregister happened to point.  The archive's own build took a bus error atthe first file it accepted from $HOME/.SCREENS, which is the only thingthe program is for; on the machine it was written on the registerevidently held something harmless.  One line; nothing else is changed.Built trap-free (-qm), so it needs no cio.  With $HOME/.SCREENS/hiholding a command line, it runs it (tools/datatests/PA.cases).